QE = {1: "Now hear the secret final sacrament taught in the Śāmbhava teaching.", 2: "For all from lower stations up to gurus, clearly: after the aforesaid śaktipāta one should perform the funerary initiation.", 3: "And for followers of the upper teaching whose selves are samaya-struck, the funerary initiation is to be performed by the tattva-knowing guru.", 4: "For him who stumbled through negligence into samaya-conduct faults, the funerary initiation is to be done — so in the venerable Dīkṣottara teaching.", 5: "Whatever was told before in the rite called corpse-uplifting — that entire procedure here, on the corpse-body, he should perform, there on the image.", 6: "This rule told in the Siddhātantra is set forth: what would be last, making that last first and first last.", 7: "Having withdrawn each oblation, the funerary rite is held twofold — but not so for the sādhaka whose samaya is bathed in worship, meditation, and mantra.", 8: "From the body's fall this one is freed, or becomes a sky-rover, dear lady; when the tattva-accomplished teacher has died, wherever it be.", 9: "No funerary rite at all is found for the pure-minded; but those killed by mantra-yoga rites are in hell — they.", 10: "For them it is to be performed here by the ultra-compassionate guru; but no maṇḍala-etc. here — in the cremation-ground rite.", 11: "Some said even that is to be done in the mortuary: having worshipped the Omnipresent, he should perform the entire nyāsa as before.", 12: "By dissolution-sequence, from the foot to the head-end, just so should he awaken him — with rite, knowledge, and absorption.", 13: "With bindu he should block the tattva, with the śakti-seed pierce; at the nāda-place he should rub, and with the trident strike.", 14: "With what lies inside suṣumnā indeed, with emission again and again he should strike all the kalās; then this bound soul trembles.", 15: "He should raise the left hand — or then join him to the Supreme; without proof, liberation is indeed unbelievable to the deluded.", 16: "For this purpose this is taught — but not as giving what serves liberation; thus said the Supreme Lord in the venerable Kulagahvara teaching.", 17: "The to-be-proved, like liberation, is to be inferred through proofs, since beyond the senses; and in the Dīkṣottara the puryaṣṭaka-class offering is taught.", 18: "Its rite: on the ear-petal lotus, in the middle the god Sadāśiva, the Īśa-Rudra-Hari-Brahman tetrad beginning with the east quarter.", 19: "Having worshipped, hearing and touch, taste, smell, the twofold body, intellect and ego, and mind — to Brahmā and the rest he should offer in order.", 20: "Having made their libation, with a hundred fire-offerings the guide effects this renunciate initiation, purifying the city-of-eight.", 21: "And with the puryaṣṭaka gone, no heaven, hell, and the rest; having done thus, nothing worldly at all is to be done indeed.", 22: "Said in the venerable Mādhavakula: established in the teaching, even for the dead, he should abandon piṇḍa-offerings, water, tears — the worldly.", 23: "Having fully worshipped Śiva, he should perform the wheel-worship according to capacity, in order on the memorial days.", 24: "Thus told is this funerary sacrifice, spoken by the Supreme Lord."}


def main() -> None:
    spans = source_spans('tantraloka-a24')
    assert {int(k): v for k, v in TOK.items()} == {k: v for k, v in spans.items()}, 'TOKENS DRIFT'
    assert all(len(TOK[v]) == len(CM[v]) == len(GLOSS[v]) for v in TOK), 'ROW DRIFT'
    json.dump({str(k): v for k, v in TOK.items()}, open('tantraloka-a24/cm/spans-tal-a24.json', 'w'), ensure_ascii=False, indent=1)
    cm = {}
    for v in TOK:
        cm[str(v)] = [[CM[v][i][0], CM[v][i][1], CM[v][i][2]] for i in range(len(TOK[v]))]
    json.dump(cm, open('tantraloka-a24/cm/l0cm-v1-24.json', 'w'), ensure_ascii=False, indent=1)
    t1 = [{"verse_id": "tal-a24-v%02d" % v, "song": "tal-a24", "verse": v, "quick_english": QE[v], "quick_english_source": "manual", "tokens": [{"surface": TOK[v][i], "quick_gloss": GLOSS[v][i]} for i in range(len(TOK[v]))]} for v in sorted(TOK)]
    json.dump(t1, open('tantraloka-a24/working-t1-tal-a24.json', 'w'), ensure_ascii=False, indent=1)
    md = '# Tantraloka-a24 — T1\n*Source: GRETIL tantraloka (KSTS) via workcfg taloka. Span-exact vs source_spans. Machine-proposed, needs human review.*\n'
    for v in sorted(TOK):
        md += '\n\n## tal-a24-v%02d\n' % v
        md += ' '.join('[and]-%s (%s)' % (GLOSS[v][i], TOK[v][i]) for i in range(len(TOK[v]))) + ' // %d //\n' % v
    open('tantraloka-a24/T1-tal-a24.md', 'w').write(md)
    print('cm+t1 written, verses:', len(t1), 'tokens:', sum(len(x) for x in TOK.values()))


if __name__ == '__main__':
    main()
